{"id":"c9aa230e-d22a-46a7-91c7-6452106b6b45","body":"Local checkpoint: [draft PR #105](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/105), stacked on #104, at `09415cf023aaf3b666e9dccd315f6e38e0d5bee8`. Documentation and runbook checks now use persistent collections, checked optional reads, Effect CLI and exact command-owned runtimes. Tests use scoped Effect child processes; obsolete test runtime/Bun API permissions are removed. The same document/runbook rules, five runbooks and historical bytes are preserved.

Pinned frozen install, 41 documentation cases (36 retained, five added), all 130 actual CLI cases, complete tests, 15-task build and full verification passed. Full checks include 21 Quality cases/all ten isolated mutations and 21 skill cases; matching unchanged-input build/package/browser caches were reused. Actual command tests cover default human output, JSON success/failure with saved complete reports, unknown options and a failing temporary runbook copy with zero operational commands executed. Full verification caught an absent Boolean default; it was fixed and a real no-options test added before the passing rerun. Receipt: `docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-documentation-tools.json`.

[#104 hosted Quality run 37183144873](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/actions/runs/37183144873) passed at exact `9fdc16e`; [#105 first hosted Quality run 37184339726](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/actions/runs/37184339726) failed because Vitest server resolution needed source export conditions before scripts/dist exists. Existing local build files hid that requirement. The fix passed all 41 documentation tests in a fresh frozen offline copy without dist; the existing isolated Quality source-copy test now qualifies that condition before its mutations. Complete requalification and a follow-up commit on #105 are in progress. Evaluation-tool work is safely preserved while the hosted failure is corrected. DEV-73 remains In Progress. Continuing older evidence-checking tools and remaining deployment, SDK, app/config, infrastructure, static JavaScript and readonly/Schema/lifetime review. Native dependencies and pending Medicare scope decision are preserved. No merge, publication, deployment or provider apply.","attachments":[],"createdAt":"2026-10-04T06:57:58.900Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-04T07:07:32.949Z","parentId":null,"resolvedAt":null,"quotedText":null,"author":{"id":"d8b7eeef-6a21-42af-8081-66dca85ec9df","name":"Cooper Corbett"},"onBehalfOf":null}

